---
// Terms of sale and use. The rules mirror docs/release-and-licensing.md and
// the vocabulary in GLOSSARY.md; change those first, then this page.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Marker from '../components/Marker.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for buying and using Pocket: the License, Activations, the Trial, and who sells it."
>
  <section class="container page">
    <Marker shape="square" play />
    <h1 class="h indent">Terms</h1>
    <div class="indent prose">
    <p class="label muted">Last updated: November 23, 2026</p>

    <p>
      These terms apply when you download, try, buy or use Pocket, a movable, resizable widget
      for the Mac. By using Pocket you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use
      Pocket.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Pocket is made and sold by dk2la, an individual based in France. For any question about
      Pocket or these terms, write to
      <a href="mailto:support@pocketwidget.tech">support@pocketwidget.tech</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What Pocket does</h2>
    <p>
      Pocket is a widget that stays on your desktop and holds your calendar, mail, notes,
      clipboard, music, timers, files and an optional AI Assistant. Some features need
      permissions that macOS asks you for, and you can turn each one off later in System
      Settings:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Calendars, to show and edit your events;</li>
      <li>Microphone and Speech Recognition, to dictate, only while you are dictating;</li>
      <li>Automation of Spotify and Music, to control what is playing;</li>
      <li>Accessibility, to move and resize other apps' windows into layouts.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      What Pocket does with your data is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy
      Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can use Pocket</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use Pocket where the law, sanctions or export rules forbid it.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Orders are handled by Polar, our merchant of record. Polar processes your
      payment, collects any taxes that apply, handles refunds and issues your License key. Its
      own terms apply to the payment itself.
    </p>

    <h2>The Trial</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The Trial lasts 3 days from the first launch of Pocket and includes every feature.</li>
      <li>Starting the Trial needs an internet connection.</li>
      <li>There is one Trial per Mac. Reinstalling Pocket does not restart it.</li>
      <li>
        When the Trial ends and you have no License, Pocket locks until you enter a License key.
        Your settings and data stay intact.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The License</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A License is permanent. You pay once: $24, or $19 while a launch price applies. The
        price shown at checkout is the one you pay.
      </li>
      <li>
        A License includes every future feature of Pocket except Subscription features (see
        below).
      </li>
      <li>
        One License key is for one person. Please don't share, resell or publish it.
      </li>
      <li>
        A License allows up to 3 Activations. An Activation links your License to one Mac. You
        can remove an Activation in Pocket to move it to another Mac.
      </li>
      <li>
        Pocket checks your License key online about once a day. Without a connection it keeps
        working for up to 7 days after the last successful check, then asks you to reconnect.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A License gives you the right to use Pocket. Pocket itself, including its code and
      design, remains the property of dk2la. Don't copy or redistribute it, and don't work
      around the Trial or License checks, except where the law gives you that right.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a License key is shared, published or used to get around these limits, we may disable
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>Installing and updating</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You may install Pocket on Macs you own or control. Without a License it runs for the
        Trial only.
      </li>
      <li>
        Pocket checks for updates about once a day and asks you before installing one. Updates
        fix bugs, close security holes and add features.
      </li>
      <li>
        To remove Pocket, quit it and drag it from Applications to the Trash. The
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how to remove the data it leaves behind.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Subscription features</h2>
    <p>
      We may later add Subscription features: features that need a separate, recurring
      Subscription even if you hold a License. No Subscription exists today. If one is
      introduced, it will be optional and will not remove anything your License already
      includes.
    </p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      You can get a refund within 14 days of purchase if your License key was never activated.
      The details are in the <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content and the Assistant</h2>
    <p>
      Your mail, notes, events and everything else you keep in Pocket stay yours. We don't
      receive them and claim no rights in them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Assistant's answers come from the AI provider you connect, not from us. They can be
      wrong, incomplete or out of date, and they are not professional advice. Check them
      before you rely on them. You are responsible for what you do with Pocket, such as the
      emails you send, the events you change and the playbooks you run.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Pocket works with services run by other companies: your mail provider, the AI provider
      you connect, Spotify, Apple and Polar. Their own terms apply when you use them, and we
      are not responsible for how they work or for their being available.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair use</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use Pocket to break the law, to send spam or harmful messages, to infringe other
      people's rights, or to harm Pocket, its servers or its users.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what data Pocket and this website
      handle.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates and changes</h2>
    <p>
      We improve Pocket over time, so features may be added, changed or removed. We may also
      update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version. A change to these terms
      does not take away a License you already hold.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using Pocket at any time by removing it. If you break these terms, for
      example by sharing your License key, we may disable your License. Where the law
      requires it, we will tell you first and give you a chance to fix the problem.
    </p>

    <h2>Warranty</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep Pocket reliable, but we provide it as it is. We don't promise that it will
      be free of errors, that it will never be interrupted, or that it will work with every
      version of macOS or every other app. The 3-day Trial is there so you can check that Pocket
      suits you before you buy.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      As far as the law allows, dk2la is not liable for indirect losses such as lost data, lost
      profits or business interruption, and our total liability to you is limited to the amount
      you paid for your License.
    </p>

    <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms limits rights that the law gives you and that cannot be waived or
      limited by contract. This includes the legal guarantees that consumers have in their
      country of residence, and our liability where the law does not allow it to be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by French law. If you are a consumer, you also keep the
      protection of the mandatory consumer laws of the country where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:support@pocketwidget.tech">support@pocketwidget.tech</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
